  "prefLabel": "He-P 4043.05 General Requirements for Non-Healing Arts Radiation Generating Devices (RGD)",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "He-P 4043.05 General Requirements for Non-Healing Arts Radiation Generating Devices (RGD).\n\n(a) Unless otherwise provided in this Part, this section applies to all RGDs and certified and certifiable cabinet x-ray systems, both of which shall also meet the requirements of 21 CFR 1020.40.\n\n(b) Warning devices shall:\n\n(1) Be labeled so that their purpose is easily identified; and\n\n(2) Contain an easily visible warning light labeled with the words \"X-RAY ON\" or other words having a similar intent. This warning light shall be located near any switch that energizes an x-ray tube and shall be illuminated only when the tube is energized and be of a fail-safe design.\n\n(c) All RGD equipment labeling shall include:\n\n(1) A readily visible and discernible sign or signs bearing the radiation symbol in accordance with He-P 4022.11 and the words: “CAUTION RADIATION - THIS EQUIPMENT PRODUCES RADIATION WHEN ENERGIZED,” or words having a similar intent, near any\n\nswitch that energizes an x-ray tube; and\n\n(2) For RGDs with designed openings for object entries such as baggage units, the following language shall be posted at or near each opening: “CAUTION – X-RAY HAZARD: DO NOT INSERT ANY PART OF THE BODY WHEN SYSTEM IS ENERGIZED”, or words having similar intent.\n\n(d) Each x-ray tube housing shall be subject to the following requirements:\n\n(1) When the x-ray tube housing is the primary shielding for the x-ray tube, and is intended to be opened for normal use or maintenance, the housing shall be equipped with an interlock that shuts off the high voltage to the x-ray tube if the housing is opened; and\n\n(2) Each x-ray tube housing shall be so constructed that, with all shutters closed, the leakage radiation measured at a distance of 5 centimeters from the x-ray tube housing surface does not exceed 0.025 mSv (2.5 mrem) per hour. This limit shall be met at the maximum tube rating.\n\n(e) Each x-ray generator or high-voltage source shall be supplied with a protective cabinet which limits leakage radiation to 2.5 µSv (0.25 mrem) per hour at a distance of 5 centimeters measured at the nearest accessible surface.\n\n(f) For closed-beam systems, the requirements in He-P 4043.05(d)(2) and 4043.05(e) shall be met by complying with He-P 4043.08(e).\n\n(g) For an RGD in a shielded room, the requirements in He-P 4043.05(d)(2) and 4043.05(e) shall be met by measuring from any accessible surface outside the room housing the RGD.\n\n(h) For hand-held, open-beam RGDs, the requirements in He-P 4043.05(d)(2) and 4043.05(e) shall be met by complying with the limits in He-P 4043.10(c).\n\n(i) Radiation surveys of all RGDs shall be sufficient to show compliance with radiation emission requirements of this Part, and as required by He-P 4020.05, entitled “Occupational Dose Limits for Adults” and He-P 4020.13, entitled “Dose Limits for Individual Members of the Public”. At a minimum, surveys shall be performed:\n\n(1) Upon installation of the equipment, and at least once every 12 months thereafter;\n\n(2) Following any change in the initial arrangement, number, or type of local components in the system;\n\n(3) Following any maintenance requiring the disassembly, removal, or repair of a local component in the system;\n\n(4) During the performance of maintenance, calibration, and other procedures if the procedures require the presence of a primary x-ray beam while any local component in the system is disassembled or removed;\n\n(5) Post bypass of a safety device or interlock as required by He-P 4043.06(a)-(f);\n\n(6) Any time a visual inspection of the local components in the system reveals an abnormal condition; and\n\n(7) Whenever a personnel monitoring device shows a significant increase over previous monitoring period or readings are approaching the limits specified in He-P 4020.05.\n\n(j) Radiation survey measurements shall not be required if a registrant can otherwise demonstrate compliance with the requirements of this Part to the satisfaction of the department of health and human services radiological health section (DHHS/RHS).\n\n(k) Each area or room containing an RGD where an individual might receive 0.02 mSv (2 mrem) in any one hour or 1 mSv (100 mrem) per year shall be conspicuously posted with a sign or signs bearing the radiation symbol and the words “CAUTION - X-RAY EQUIPMENT,” “CAUTION – RADIATION GENERATING DEVICE”, or words having a similar intent.\n\n(l) RGDs shall be secured in such a way as to be accessible to, or operable by, only authorized personnel when not in operation.\n\nSource. #6827, eff 8-6-98; ss by #8692, INTERIM, eff 7-27-06, EXPIRES: 2-2-07; ss by #8808, eff 1-24-07; ss by #10804, eff 3-26-15; ss by #14336, eff 8-8-25, EXPIRES: 8-8-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-p4040-4061.html"
